Subject: [PATCH] refactor: rename app/admin -> app/account
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The 'admin' folder held no privileged/operator functionality — it was
already per-user self-service endpoints (/me/keys, /me/gateway-tokens)
protected by regular JWT auth (get_current_user), not by the unused
ADMIN_API_KEY / require_admin dependency. The naming was misleading:
it suggested superuser-only operations that don't exist here.

- app/admin/ -> app/account/
- app/admin/router.py -> app/account/keys_router.py (name now matches
  its actual content: CRUD + health-check + usage stats for the
  caller's own API keys)
- gateway_tokens_router.py keeps its name, only moves folder
- tests/admin/ -> tests/account/, imports updated accordingly
- app/main.py: admin_router -> keys_router (import + include_router)
- app/tokens/models.py: fixed a stale comment claiming ADMIN_API_KEY
  guards '/admin/*' endpoints — it doesn't guard anything right now;
  require_admin (kept as-is in app/account/dependencies.py) is unused,
  reserved for a possible future cross-account operator feature

require_admin / ADMIN_API_KEY themselves are untouched — still dead
code, still not wired to any router. Renamed with them rather than
deleted, since that's a separate decision.

All 116 existing tests pass unchanged.
